{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/556782-designing-malfeans","id":556782,"title":"Designing Malfeans","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-16T05:39:37-07:00","id":556782,"title":"Designing Malfeans","content":"Greetings fellow pre-Restless!<br /> <br /> I intend to run a Doomslayers Chronicle (using Psyches, not Shadow-eaten) soonish. Its a great setting, and offers a very in-universe way to switch from action to contemplation on the spot (due to the Labyrinth and its nature). <br /> <br /> For that reason, I need some driving antagonists and personalities in the form of Malfeans. I am planning to steal the Siege Tower Of Entropy from Planescape Torment as the passive, non-malicious aspect of Oblivion, the Barrow of all Barrow, who simply unmakes. I want to present him as a sort of natural force, something that needs to be feared, but needs to be opposed because things that are have a need to be, and Entropy is fundamentally opposed to that. <br /> <br /> However, I need some other antagonists and philosophies to showcase. Do you, fellow forumites, have any in mind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T15:14:11-07:00","id":558790,"title":"","content":"The Wraith Project has a sourcebook on Malfean creation. I think it's mirrored somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T03:02:00-07:00","id":559193,"title":"","content":"That site does indeed rock<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Did you mean the article &quot;Dark Gods Awaken&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.cattail.nu/wraithproject/main.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.cattail.nu/wraithproject/main.html\" target=\"_blank\"> The Wraith Project </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.cattail.nu/wraithproject/main.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.cattail.nu/wraithproject/main.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> ghosts, Wraith, Abyssals, Orpheus, White Wolf, World of Darkness, RPG </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5238,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","user":"Herbert_West","date":". 06-18-2015, 06:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T20:34:55-07:00","id":560283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/556782-designing-malfeans?p=559193#post559193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That site does indeed rock. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Did you mean the article &quot;Dark Gods Awaken&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.cattail.nu/wraithproject/main.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.cattail.nu/wraithproject/main.html\" target=\"_blank\"> The Wraith Project </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.cattail.nu/wraithproject/main.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.cattail.nu/wraithproject/main.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> ghosts, Wraith, Abyssals, Orpheus, White Wolf, World of Darkness, RPG </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> More precisely, this perhaps? <a href=\"http://www.cattail.nu/wraithproject/archives/0111malfeans.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.cattail.nu/wraithproject/...1malfeans.html</a><br /> Pardon me if i erred out of ignorance...<br /> <br /> As an aside, is there any examples of stated-out Malfeans/Neverborn in the books, either Wraith or Orpheus?<br /> I'm interested for the sake of reference, dealing of late with trying to port something from (way) early books and i'm somewhat divided between working on it as an Incarna as implied or something closer to the Underworld as implied by a number of little peculiarities (the source is most certainly pre-Wraith, pre-Mage too for that matter).<br /> <br /> PS: Not a question i would usually make (at all) - but have the Fallen or Earthbound been described as connected with/imprisoned into the Underworld or Labyrinth anywhere in fluff? Though not usually my cup of tea, it might be relevant to my interest this time around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-18-2015, 11:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T03:59:01-07:00","id":560611,"title":"","content":"That link doesn't work for me and I can't find it. Maybe it was on Ex Libris Nocturnis instead? I'll check my files next week when I get home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T01:04:30-07:00","id":561664,"title":"","content":"<i>End Game</i> has a relatively minor Malfean statted out. It in no way lives up to the hype.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T03:01:02-07:00","id":561741,"title":"","content":"Coldheart gets stats in Ends of Empire, as a relatively powerful spectre, but he's nowhere near Neverborn status. The thing is, though, Neverborn (until Orpheus) are primal forces of anti-Creation. They don't have stats because it'd be like statting out the Wyrm. If you get into a fight with a Malfean, you're doing it wrong. <br /> <br /> As it happens, the Fallen are said to be imprisoned in/near/adjacent to/beneath the Labyrinth in the Abyss. It's worth mentioning, however, that the Labyrinth has analogues in various levels of reality, as it's connected to Malfeas and other labyrinthine realms, which could merely mean that the Abyss is connected to the Labyrinth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T06:44:59-07:00","id":561845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/556782-designing-malfeans?p=560283#post560283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> More precisely, this perhaps? <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://www.cattail.nu/wraithproject/archives/0111malfeans.html&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.cattail.nu/wraithproject/...1malfeans.html</a><br /> Pardon me if i erred out of ignorance...<br /> <br /> As an aside, is there any examples of stated-out Malfeans/Neverborn in the books, either Wraith or Orpheus?</div> </div> </div> </div>Found it! This was so hard to find (I printscreened it as a PDF): <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20041123201219/http://www.nocturnis.net/articles/wraith/default/2004/February/printfriendly/401/page1.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://web.archive.org/web/200411232...401/page1.html</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T06:47:04-07:00","id":561846,"title":"","content":"I'd add that the rules above seem most fitting for Onceborn, rather than Neverborn, as it stats out wraiths who become Malfeans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T00:06:49-07:00","id":562716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/556782-designing-malfeans?p=561664#post561664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>End Game</i> has a relatively minor Malfean statted out. It in no way lives up to the hype.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would guess so - what page?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T08:19:45-07:00","id":564139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/556782-designing-malfeans?p=561845#post561845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Found it! This was so hard to find (I printscreened it as a PDF): <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20041123201219/http://www.nocturnis.net/articles/wraith/default/2004/February/printfriendly/401/page1.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://web.archive.org/web/200411232...401/page1.html</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Wow, thanks. Do you happen to have a good mirror link for the rest of their stuff? All of it seems very awesome<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> W.r.t Gorool, I always read that as him being merely a very, very powerful Shadow, sort of like the Phasiphae (sic?) of the Ferrymen, as he is but part of Charon. To be a Neverborn, he'd need to be something that was created just at Creation, and to be a Onceborn, he'd need to be a full ex-Wraith devoured by his Shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T01:44:27-07:00","id":565120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Wow, thanks. Do you happen to have a good mirror link for the rest of their stuff? All of it seems very awesome<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> W.r.t Gorool, I always read that as him being merely a very, very powerful Shadow, sort of like the Phasiphae (sic?) of the Ferrymen, as he is but part of Charon. To be a Neverborn, he'd need to be something that was created just at Creation, and to be a Onceborn, he'd need to be a full ex-Wraith devoured by his Shadow. </div> </div> </div>The fluff unfortunately identifies him as one of the most powerful Neverborn. Which sadly makes the Neverborn a whole lot less scary, as Gorool always struck me as Godzilla in the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T03:55:05-07:00","id":565168,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm going to invoke The Golden Rule, as him being a Neverborn <b>makes no sense at all</b>. That would make a part of a Wraith older than the Wraith, and possibly the Universe. Alternatively, Gorool is _not_ Charon's Shadow, but a minor Neverborn that munched his Shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T13:16:10-07:00","id":565693,"title":"","content":"I believe the latter, that Gorool was one who did munch on Charon's Shadow is infact the case, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T17:04:27-07:00","id":565867,"title":"","content":"Yeah, he swallowed Charon's shadow but was a Neverborn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T02:54:11-07:00","id":567612,"title":"","content":"I see.<br /> <br /> Sidenote: do you think that presenting Oblivion (as in, the thing and &quot;actor&quot;) itself as non-malicious would fit with Wraith? I'm currently thinking of spinning it in a way that the malicious, decay-focused, corrupting aspect is only there because Wraiths, as beings of memory and rememberance, want it to be. Frankly, by expecting dissolution to be something bad, we made it bad. I might even spin it so as to make Oblivion and Transcendence one and the same, the only difference being if you are not OK with being unmade as opposed to being OK.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T09:28:47-07:00","id":568075,"title":"","content":"In a way, it is fairly simple to spin Oblivion that way, there are quotes abound that basically explain that it's basically doing what it's meant to be doing, clearing up the old so the new can be born and is a passive function of the Universe. Shadows are essentially the demons in Jacob's Ladder, there to forcefully tear a person's clinging remnants of the world of the living, so they can Transcend in peace... A cruel kindness to force the Wraith's hand, basically.<br /> <br /> Now when I talk more on Transcendance onwards, let me say in this context it's more the point of a Wraith being removed from the Underworld, either by Transcending or being wiped out by Oblivion in a Harrowing.<br /> <br /> Spectres come when the Shadow puts too much Permanent Angst (the wraith's measure of feelings of despair, hopelessness and also <i>sympathy with Oblivion</i>) on their Wraith, essentially a permanent version of Catharsis. Catharsis if taken by the name, is an act of purification and cleansing of the mind and/or body, &quot;of blowing off pent-up steam&quot;... The Shadow takes direct control to let the Wraith let go of what's holding them back, prodding them towards Transcendance. The act itself can be harsh, but it's done to clear up it's target.<br /> <br /> Being a Spectre may be seen as an antithesis of what a Shadow is meant to do, as a Spectre cannot Transcend, though those who are Shadow-Eaten can sure go on to do their destruction of Passions and Fetters on other Wraiths, keeping the goal ongoing. They know all what buttons to press to achieve their cruel kindness too, being linked to the hive-mind and other wraith's Shadows. They have given up their path to Transcendance to help as many other Wraiths instead.<br /> <br /> I do not see Transcendance and Oblivion as the same, though they are close.<br /> Oblivion wipes out Corpus and puts it down into it's main elements from which new things can form in it's place. It's not a place where new things are born from, though it wipes out stagnation from the table and so is an enabling factor for the world to fit new things and to move onwards. I believe Transcendance originally led to Lethe, of Exalted... Where ghosts were sent for reincarnation.<br /> In the old world of darkness though, that may not be the case as it seems more now that a Wraith who Transcends will have their soul collected for God's plan of a new universe... However that aspect of the metaplot and just where the Scarlet Phoenix and Ebon Dragon (The Last living Angels) sit. Also note that Charon fell into Oblivion and was somehow reincarnated through elaborate working of what must have been a rather unique Harrowing... Though I think this is down to him making a Fetter of the world and he thus resolved it in saving the day against the Sixth Great Maelstrom upon his return.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}